1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,520
Nasal polyps, if congestion and smell loss keep coming back, this might not be simple allergies.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:10,720
Nasal polyps are soft growths from long-term inflammation in your nasal and sinus lining.

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:15,920
They're more common in people with asthma, allergies, or a sensitivity to certain pain relievers.

4
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,000
A few habits can make them worse.

5
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:22,960
First, taking aspirin, ibuprofen, or naproxen without knowing your sensitivity.

6
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:28,960
Some people have a reaction called AERD, where these drugs suddenly worsen congestion.

7
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:33,680
Talk to your doctor about acetaminophen instead, and mention any drug reactions.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,280
Second, breathing in tobacco smoke, chemical fumes, or dust without protection keeps the swelling and inflammation going.

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,360
Try an air purifier indoors and a mask around fumes or dust.

10
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,280
Last, skipping saline rinse and letting mucus sit lets irritation keep polyps growing.

11
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,760
Use a saline rinse once or twice a day, and run a humidifier at home.

12
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:01,120
Watching pain reliever choices, limiting irritants, and saline rinsing may genuinely help.

13
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:06,720
If congestion or smell loss lasts more than 2 weeks, an ENT visit is worth considering.
